--
-- Name: TABLE ireports360_parity_windows; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: postgres
--

COMMENT ON TABLE public.ireports360_parity_windows IS 'Latest parity verification of each 30-day window of iReports360 history against the vendor API. Written by runIReports360ParitySweep. A window whose checked_at is older than ~21 days means the sweep itself has stopped running, not that the rotation is mid-cycle — with ~8 windows and one run a day, full coverage takes ~8 days.';

--
-- Name: COLUMN ireports360_parity_windows.extra_in_mirror; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: postgres
--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ireports360_parity_windows.extra_in_mirror IS 'Rows the mirror holds that the CRM did not return for this window. NOT automatically deleted when it exceeds half the window (see decideParityAction) — at that size the likeliest explanation is a truncated vendor response, and deleting settled history on a bad fetch is unrecoverable because the CRM would have to still be serving those rows to restore them.';

