--
-- Name: TABLE sensitive_data_access_audit; Type: COMMENT; Schema: public; Owner: postgres
--

COMMENT ON TABLE public.sensitive_data_access_audit IS 'INERT -- 0 rows, ever, and the identity sequence has never been called. THIS TABLE IS NOT EVIDENCE THAT NOBODY HAS READ SENSITIVE DATA; it is evidence that its write path is never travelled. That path is public.v_employee_locations_masked, whose WHERE clause calls private.log_sensitive_data_access_event() per row -- and no application code selects that view. Nine files read public.employee_locations directly through the service-role client instead. The writer is functional (verified on staging 2026-09-06), just unused. Do NOT answer "who read employee data?" from this table: public.audit_logs records actions and writes, not reads, so that question currently has no source. Owner decision 2026-09-06: label, do not wire or drop.';

